power: supply: bq256xx: notify after a successful charge switch

U30 Air's SGM41513 has no charger IRQ. A userspace pause/resume changes the
hardware and chg_off, but without a power_supply notification the FGU and
charging LED can retain the previous state until their safety deadline.
Publish the successful change after updating the saved charging choice;
failed writes must not notify or change that choice. Keep charging policy,
Type-C roles and the existing event consumers unchanged.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -1008,6 +1008,7 @@
 			return ret;
 		/* "N/A" stops charging until "Fast" (or "Trickle"), also across plugs (bq2560x_chg_detect) */
 		WRITE_ONCE(bq->chg_off, val->intval == POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_NONE);
+		power_supply_changed(psy);
 		break;
 
 	default:
